WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
One other letter that you will need to pay attention to in the texts in the book is G.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:13.200
At the beginning of a word, where it occurs only rarely, and after N in the middle of a word, it has the sound of English G.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:23.200
When it occurs between vowels in the middle of a word, however, it may have the sound of English H or the sound of CH in the Scottish pronunciation of loch.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.400
Practice these differences in the following:

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.000
The name Gandhi.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
காந்தி (Gaandhi)

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.000
There.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
அங்கே (Angee)

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Son.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
மகன் (Magan)

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Happiness.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.500
மகிழ்ச்சி (Magiẓchi)